<title>USA: Hershey Foods sells $150 mln 10-year notes.</title>
<headline>Hershey Foods sells $150 mln 10-year notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Hershey Foods Corp was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Hershey Foods, based in Hershey, Pennsylvania, is the top producer of chocolate and other confections in the U.S.</p>
<p>BORROWER HERSHEY FOODS CORP</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 6.95 PCT   MATURITY 3/01/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.698  FIRST PAY DATE 9/01/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 6.992 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AA-MINUS  SPREAD 40 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
